# This project must never store CRLF. GCS writes LF-only, tab-indented UTF-8 and
# its serialization contract depends on it (docs/02-gcs-format.md 2.1); the
# byte-exactness tests compare fixture bytes directly, so a CRLF checkout would
# fail them for reasons unrelated to the code. Note that the upstream clones in
# gcs/ and gurps/ are checked out with core.autocrlf and *do* have CRLF working
# trees — always take fixtures from their git blobs, never their working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# GCS data files, spelled out so intent survives any future change to the above.
*.gcs text eol=lf
*.eqp text eol=lf
*.adq text eol=lf
*.skl text eol=lf
*.not text eol=lf
*.spl text eol=lf
*.gct text eol=lf

# Binary, so git never touches them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
